# Cut the full-text search claim — search has NEVER worked (DRAFT, operator approval required)
#
# *** APPLIES ON TOP OF README-COMBINED-apply-all.patch (or the five separate patches). ***
#
# FTSBody is declared at internal/agent/agent.go:66 and read at internal/background/
# indexer.go:114-115 — and ASSIGNED NOWHERE. I grepped every assignment form across the whole
# repo, tests included: zero results. So `if s.FTSBody != ""` is never true, UpsertFTS is
# never called, and the session_fts virtual table stays empty forever.
#
# Production confirms it: 56 indexed sessions, ZERO fts rows, for months. The indexer itself
# works correctly — only the FTS half is dead, which is why reading indexer.go shows what
# looks like working search machinery.
#
# The demonstration that settles it (Developer Advocate): the session list DISPLAYS the string
# "MEMORY-TOKEN-7731 the capital of the demo is Coralville", and searching q=Coralville returns
# 0 hits. A string visible on screen that the product's own search cannot find.
#
# TWO EDITS:
#   :119 features row — drop "Full-text search across", keep what is true and verified.
#        Session history, auto-summaries, tags and notes all work and are visible today.
#   :135 comparison table — remove the "Search chat history" row outright. It claims a
#        capability we do not have, against competitors, which is the worst place to have one.
#        (If the comparison table is deleted wholesale per the Strategist's recommendation,
#        this hunk becomes redundant — harmless either way, but check before applying.)
#
